{"id":"9c2a9b95-b0ed-491b-a10b-9cf428dad9af","object":"chat.completion","created":1795243696,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"SELECT ROUND(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE order_cnt >= 2) * 100.0 / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 2) AS repeat_rate\nFROM (\n  SELECT c.customer_unique_id, COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS order_cnt\n  FROM orders o\n  JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\n  WHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled', 'unavailable')\n    AND c.customer_unique_id IS NOT NULL\n  GROUP BY c.customer_unique_id\n) t;","reasoning_content":"Simple: compute repeat rate per METRIC. Need join orders to customers to get customer_unique_id, exclude canceled/unavailable, group by customer_unique_id count orders, then compute percent.\n\nNeed reference time? No time filter requested. Just overall.\n\nSQL:\nSELECT ROUND(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE order_cnt >= 2) * 100.0 / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 2) AS repeat_rate\nFROM (\n  SELECT c.customer_unique_id, COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS order_cnt\n  FROM orders o\n  JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\n  WHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled','unavailable')\n  AND c.customer_unique_id IS NOT NULL\n  GROUP BY 1\n) t;\n\nShould we exclude NULL customer_unique_id? \"默认只统计已知身份\" — yes, group by excludes nulls? No, GROUP BY includes NULL as a group. But identity NULL not merged as a person; default only count known identity. So add WHERE c.customer_unique_id IS NOT NULL.\n\nCOUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) fine since orders join to one customer each (1:1), no duplication. Actually customer_id primary key, so each order maps to exactly one customer row. Fine."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3755,"completion_tokens":387,"total_tokens":4142,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":268},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1963},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}